            },
            "createdOn": 1750319161,
            "author": {
                "name": "Kevin Tung",
                "email": "Kevin.Tung@quantatw.com",
                "username": ""
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "@paligill@gmail.com - Please confirm this is the intended design."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-harma/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/multi-gpios-sys-init",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This doesn't seem right.  Why are we writing the BIOS version into the software manager.  Shouldn't this be a read-only property?  Shouldn't the software manager _know_ what software version there is?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-harma/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/multi-gpios-sys-init",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "11110128-KevinTung",
                        "email": "kevin.wtmh@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "The legacy BIOS version path /xyz/openbmc_project/software/bios_active under the software manager does not automatically reflect the actual BIOS version. As shown in https://grok.openbmc.org/xref/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/bmc/item_updater.cpp?r=01ba956256e45b953c78591319a5f25ff4ba618d&mo=31079&fi=948#964, the default value for the xyz.openbmc_project.Software.Version interface is \"null\" unless explicitly set. Therefore, during BMC boot-up, have to write the correct BIOS version to this interface to ensure that /xyz/openbmc_project/software/bios_active exposes a meaningful and accurate version string rather than \"null\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-harma/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/multi-gpios-sys-init",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "@kevin.wtmh@gmail.com I can understand that @amithash@meta.com asked you to create the `/var/bios/host0_bios_version.txt` at BMC boot up (by reading the value from /var/lib/fb-ipmi-oem/appData.json) to cover the case where we update the BMC in production but the Host hasn't been rebooted (so no IPMI message received from Host for BIOS version). I don't see a reason for why you need to update the existing xyz.openbmc_project.Software.Version at  /xyz/openbmc_project/software/bios_active? In my understanding this is not needed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-harma/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/multi-gpios-sys-init",
                    "line": 34,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "11110128-KevinTung",
                        "email": "kevin.wtmh@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Understood. I\u2019ve updated to only create /var/bios/host0_bios_version.txt from the legacy appData.json."
                }
            ],
